cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Chemistry Data Extractor Toolkit
message: >-
  If you use this software in work that you publish, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Battulga
    given-names: Enkhnyam
    affiliation: RWTH Aachen University
repository-code: https://github.com/Enkhnyam/chemistry-data-extractor-toolkit
abstract: >-
  A local tool for building auditable experimental datasets from scientific PDFs. One language
  model extracts records against a schema you define; a second re-reads the paper and audits
  every record against it; the reviewer checks what remains with the source text alongside and
  the passage behind each value highlighted. Schema, prompts and worked examples are
  configuration rather than code, so the same pipeline serves any chemistry. Generalised from a
  PET-depolymerisation database built the same way.
keywords:
  - information extraction
  - large language models
  - chemistry
  - literature mining
  - LLM-as-a-judge
  - research data
license: MIT
